.TH GHIDRA-REPORT 1 "September 2026" "ghidra-report v0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ghidra-report \- automated binary analysis, threat triage, and firmware carving toolkit powered by Ghidra
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ghidra-report.sh
[\fIBINARY_FILE\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B ghidra-report.sh
.B \-\s-1\-\s0batch
[\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B ghidra-report.sh
.B \-\s-1\-\s0watch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B ghidra-report.sh
.B \-\s-1\-\s0diff
\fIREPORT_A.json\fR \fIREPORT_B.json\fR
.br
.B ghidra-report.sh
.B \-\s-1\-\s0carve
\fIFIRMWARE_FILE\fR [\fIOUTPUT_DIR\fR]
.br
.B ghidra-report.sh
.B \-\s-1\-\s0dashboard
[\fIPORT\fR]
.br
.B ghidra-report.sh
.B \-\s-1\-\s0search
\fITERM\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ghidra-report
is an automated headless analysis harness for Ghidra. It ingests compiled executables (PE, ELF, Mach-O), embedded firmware containers, and retro ROMs (Super Nintendo 65816), executing static analysis, Shannon entropy evaluation, shellcode stub detection, MITRE ATT&CK capability mapping, P-code emulation, and cross-reference tracing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0format " <txt|json|md|html|sarif|yar|misp|all>"
Select output report formats. Defaults to \fBall\fR (generates 7 artifacts).
.TP
.BI \-j ", " \-\s-1\-\s0parallel " [N]"
Dispatch concurrent analysis workers across N CPU threads for batch jobs.
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0findcrypt
Scan binary memory for 124+ cryptographic constants (AES, ChaCha, MD5, SHA-256, RC4, TEA, Blowfish) and tag discovered algorithms in Ghidra bookmarks.
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0detect-type " <FILE>"
Inspect and print the auto-detected binary format (PE, ELF, GBA, N64, PSX, SNES, raw) without initiating a full project build.
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0webhook " <URL>"
Send notification alerts upon analysis completion to Slack, Discord, or generic Webhooks.
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0carve " <FILE> [OUT_DIR]"
Deep boundary scanner and carving pipeline for embedded firmware containers (SquashFS, CRAMFS, JFFS2, U-Boot uImage, GZIP, and embedded ELFs).
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0diff " <A.json> <B.json>"
Semantic differential analysis comparing memory layouts, entropy shifts, and API findings lifecycle ([NEW], [ABSENT], [UPDATED], [UNCHANGED]).
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0dashboard " [PORT]"
Launch the built-in dark-mode web dashboard on localhost (default: 8080).
.TP
.BI \-\s-1\-\s0search " <TERM>"
Search the SQLite report history using case-insensitive LIKE matching over report metadata, hashes, suspicious APIs, IOCs, and threat indicators, plus SQLite FTS5 over extracted/recovered strings, function names/symbols, exports, rules, capabilities, and findings stored in selected JSON report fields. Each canonical JSON report path is indexed idempotently; separate report paths with identical filenames are retained as separate records. Existing historical rows are migrated, but older text fields are available to FTS only after those report JSON files are re-indexed.
.SH RUNTIME REQUIREMENTS
The default container pins Ghidra 12.2 and JDK 25 and verifies the official Ghidra archive SHA-256 during image build. Ghidra 12.2 requires at least JDK 25. For host or Flatpak installs, use the JDK supported by that installed Ghidra release. The headless launcher prints the detected Ghidra installation path/version and Java runtime; this diagnostic does not verify that optional community loaders are installed.
.SH OUTPUT ARTIFACTS
Each analyzed input receives dedicated outputs in \fBoutput/<output_key>/\fR. The stable key contains a sanitized basename, canonical source-path hash, and content hash, so same-named inputs do not collide:
.PP
A source checkout stores writable data beside the CLI by default. Package launchers use \fB${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/ghidra-report\fR so reports and project databases are not written beneath a read-only install prefix. Set \fBGHIDRA_REPORT_DATA_DIR\fR to replace the package data root, or set \fBGHIDRA_REPORT_INGRESS_DIR\fR, \fBGHIDRA_REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR\fR, \fBGHIDRA_REPORT_PROJECTS_DIR\fR, or \fBGHIDRA_REPORT_DB_PATH\fR to override a particular location.
.PP
Exports are written to a private staging directory and moved into place only after the exporter succeeds. Each \fBreport_latest.*\fR symlink is replaced atomically, so readers do not observe a missing-link interval or a partially written linked file. The set of links for multiple formats is not switched as one transaction.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.txt
\- Full human-readable plain-text analysis report.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.json
\- Complete structured metadata and machine-readable triage dictionary.
.PP
The primary JSON report declares \fBschema_version=1.0.0\fR and is defined by \fBschemas/report-v1.schema.json\fR in the repository. The version changes when a consumer-visible contract change requires a new schema revision; additive fields may appear without removing existing fields.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.md
\- GitHub-flavored Markdown report with tables and alerts.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.html
\- Responsive, dark-mode glassmorphic HTML dashboard report.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.sarif
\- OASIS SARIF v2.1.0 JSON format for GitHub Code Scanning and CI/CD.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.yar
\- Auto-generated YARA detection rule based on imports, sections, and hashes.
.IP \(bu 2
.B report_latest.misp.json
\- MISP standard Threat Event JSON format for direct threat intel platform ingestion.
.PP
The output key can be printed with \fBpython3 scripts/project_identity.py output <binary_path>\fR. Use that key with \fB\-\-diff\fR, \fB\-\-rules\fR, or \fB\-\-trace\fR to select a specific report. A basename is accepted only when it resolves to one output directory.
.PP
Concurrent invocations that resolve to the same output identity are serialized across project import, analysis, report export, and latest-link updates. Different identities can still run in parallel. The default lock wait is 900 seconds; set \fBGHIDRA_OUTPUT_LOCK_TIMEOUT\fR to an integer between 1 and 86400 to change it. A timeout fails the run rather than allowing competing writers to proceed.
.SH AUTHOR
Google DeepMind Advanced Agentic Coding Pair Programmer.
